<title>USA: Lockheed Boeing get Hellfire work.</title>
<headline>Lockheed Boeing get Hellfire work.</headline>
<dateline>ORLANDO, Fla. 1997-04-07</dateline>
<text>
<p>Lockheed Martin Corp said Monday the U.S. Army has awarded the Hellfire Systems LLC an $83.4 million sole source contract to build an additional 1,800 Hellfire II missiles.</p>
<p>Hellfire Systems includes Lockheed Martin Electronics &amp; Missiles and Boeing Co's Autonetics &amp; Missile Systems Division. Work share will be 80 percent Lockheed Martin and 20 percent Boeing.</p>
<p>Lockheed said the production contract extends manufacturing and deliveries through September 1999.</p>
<p>((-- New York Newsdesk 212-859-1610.))</p>
